Applies on top of tools/kmc-as-pool-float.patch (independent of it: also applies straight after
tools/kmc-as-libultra-nops.patch or tools/kmc-as-hilo-libultra.patch). Game units only (--no-float-doubleword).

`li.d $fN,c` (GCC's spelling of a non-zero double literal) loaded its pool entry with `ldc1` even under
--no-float-doubleword; tools/no-float-doubleword.patch split only the explicit l.d/s.d forms. Now the pooled load
is the same lwc1 pair as l.d:
    lui $at,%hi(pool); lwc1 $fN+1,%lo(pool)($at); lwc1 $fN,%lo(pool+4)($at)
ROM evidence (asm/nonmatchings of the game units): 1028 `lui $at; lwc1; lwc1` double loads, every one with the odd
register at offset 0 first and the even register at +4 second; no ldc1 in the game code at all.

Also under --no-float-doubleword the pool entry of a double is aligned to 4 instead of 8: 489 of the 1028 distinct
addresses those ROM pairs load from are 4 mod 8 (539 are 0 mod 8). This only moves data inside the object's
.rodata; nothing reads these entries with ldc1.

Verified 2026-11-20 with the as_verify method (old = the four-patch assembler, new = all seven patches): 1181 ->
1183 matched, gained func_801CC118 (hilo patch) and func_8016A058 (this patch: case 30, `/ 5.0`), nothing lost,
no library object changed except 18020_C8EB0 (func_801CC118).

Re-apply with: git apply --ignore-whitespace tools/kmc-as-lid-pair.patch

